# CHANGELOG
##############

Version 0.4.*:
-----------
71: Every module has a useful report now, also the new one for the module eukaryote, and the rule all makes them.
    The former reports could not be built on a cluster, as their container has no LaTeX, and some of their numbers
    were wrong, or their sections always empty. Each report has the results of its tools as tables and figures, a
    methods text with versions and settings, the data written per folder, the resources requested and used per rule,
    and suggestions for config/escalation.yaml. The reads report has the samples, reads per sample and read quality.
    New container rocker/verse, key report in config/.docker.yml. New test tests/reports/run_test.sh.
    Versions 68 to 70 are still in pull request 66 and the branch real-run-kit.
67: Reworked the rules of the modules assemble, preprocess, quantify and mag_annotate and the shared
    paths and helpers. Output files stay at the same paths with the same content, see RELEASE_NOTES.
    Paths used by several rules are now defined once in folders.smk, resource blocks use
    esc("attempt", ...) and failed attempts keep their log as <log>.try<attempt>. The binners moved to
    assemble/binners/. New scripts contig_ids.py and label_binned_contigs.py replace the contig renaming
    in the assembler rules and the two MAGScoT scripts, coverm_wide_table.R and nonpareil_summary.R
    replace the two aggregate scripts, and four unused scripts and unused config keys are gone.
    MAGScoT: one hmmsearch rule for both marker sets, and it now waits for the compression of its hits.
    Fixed: the MaxBin2 clean-up used the wrong file prefix and left its side files in the bin folder,
    and the target assemble__bowtie2 asked for CRAM files also when BAM was configured.
66: Added the module eukaryote, which labels every assembly's contigs as eukaryotic or
    prokaryotic with three tools: Tiara, 4CAC (metaSPAdes assemblies only, it needs the
    assembly graph) and REMAG, and bins the eukaryotic contigs with REMAG. Each tool writes one
    table per assembly with the pipeline's contig ids (results/eukaryote/<tool>/<assembly>.tsv).
    The module is not part of 'all'; run it with the target 'eukaryote' (or eukaryote__tiara,
    eukaryote__4cac, eukaryote__remag). Settings are under 'eukaryote' in params.yaml; the
    minimum contig lengths default to 1000 bp so that fragmented (e.g. soil) assemblies can be
    classified at all.
65: Bugfix: contig_annotate__diamond__summarise now requires one DIAMOND .out per assembly
    (ASSEMBLIES), like contig_annotate__diamond does. It iterated over the sample_ids in
    SAMPLE_LIBRARY instead, so it only matched when every sample was its own assembly. With
    co-assemblies, the co-assembly's .out was never built for the summary. A sample in more
    than one assembly was listed several times. A sample that is not an assembly of its own
    (e.g. all samples in one pooled assembly) scheduled a metaspades assembly named after that
    sample, with no reads assigned to it. The R summary reads every *.out in the folder, so a
    summary is only affected if it ran before all per-assembly .out files existed. Rerun it
    in that case.
64: Bugfix: samples.tsv is now validated at startup (on the raw sheet, before the assembly_ids
    explode). A sheet with duplicate (sample_id, library_id) pairs, e.g. several lanes of a
    sample all given lib1 (what createSampleSheet.sh writes) or the Illumina S-number as
    library_id, was silently accepted: only the first row's reads were ever linked and
    processed, the other lanes were dropped, and each assembly's read list repeated that one
    library once per row. Such sheets, and sheets listing the same FASTQ on more than one row
    (in forward_filename or reverse_filename), now fail with an error listing the offending
    rows. The per-library samples.tsv lookups (reads, fastp adapters) also fail loudly now
    instead of silently taking the first match. Results from such a sheet need to be
    regenerated from scratch.
63: Added NCyc also to the contig annotate extra module, using the prodigal protein output
62: Added the tool NCyc to the pipeline (to module read_annotate_extra)
61: Accidental rerun of rules triggered by an indexing step in contig_annotate fixed (issue #47)
60: camper in mag annotate crashed in case no nvme drive was given, this is fixed now like in contig case (Issue #52)
59: In case DRAM does not find certains types, we create now empty output files to keep going (issue #44)
58: Metaspades slot system introduced (Issue #56)
57: .done-output added to mag_annotate eggnog (Issue #55)
56: Type in description fixed
55: DRAM_MAG log folder typo fixed (Issue #46)
54: Improved escalation retry handling (Issue #45)
53: The pipeline fetches now its current version from the changelog file to display instead of having it hardcoded
52: Updated the run script to avoid double definition of pipeline-folder
51: report skeletons added for all modules
50: Changed name to Snakebite-Holoruminant-MetaG
49: Moved large parts of the README.md to dedicated files located in docs/ 
48: More adjustments to dram distill output folder names
47: Added the eggnog 7 database for annotation
46: Adjusted the DRAM/distill path output for the tmp folder, which mihgt create problems on some systems.
45: Added more debug messages and graceful waiting time to rule read_annotate__kraken2__assign 
44: Turned the separate bin functions into a script file
43: Rule 'assemble__drep__separate_bins' works now more robust, important for provided assemblies
42: Changed mv command in mag_annotate__proteinortho from explicit to wildcards
41: Reverted update 40, cram stays standard, but introduced a new parameter in params where cram/bam can be chosen
40: Changed the default from cram to bam, as sometimes the header did not work
39: Removed the piping in rule assemble__bowtie2__map and split it rather in two separate steps, within the same rule though
38: Removed $TMPDIR echo from rule read_annotate__phyloflash__run
37: Removed product.html output from mag_annotate__dram_mag_distill as it is not always created
36: Added more echo messages to the logfile of assemble__bowtie2__map
35: Bugfix in assemble__bowtie2__map (missing fai index)
34: Log output added for cramToBam
33: Log output for hmmsearch added for contig annotate output
32: Diamond reports now per default only the top result
31: Harded-coded paths removed from the kegg summary R script
30: Added option to provide arbitrary named self-provided assemblies.
29: tmp folder for samtools sort adjusted to add sample_id and library_id
28: --keep-going removed from default run script
27: Critical bugfix in preprocess__bowtie2__extract_nonhost_run (crashed workflow)
26: Reversed change number 24
25: Option to provide an own, existing assembly added to the Assembler module
24: Added 'phyloflash' to Phyloflash output file, to avoid potential temp file mixups between tools
23: Improved decontamination avoiding misclassified singletons
22: Added HMMER to contig_annotate and set HydDB as starting db (issue #19)
21: Database files are now copied to avoid accidental overwriting during parallele execution (issue #18)
20: Added HydDB option as additional standard Diamond search database (issue #19)
19: Stand-alone contig_annotate__eggnog throws an error, due to an missing f-string (issue #24) 
18: Included the FastQC module for the preprocess fastqs
17: Updated the default database for Phyloflash to Silva 138.2
16: Updated the read_annotate/phyloflash docker image (downgrade spades 3.15.* to 3.14.1, spades froze often in 3.15.*)
15: Accidental overwriting of camper results and db fixed (copying removed for now, issue #18)
14: Added camper to mag_annotate from dram output
13: Output path bug in dram_mag fixed
12: Output path adjusted for phylophlan result (phylophlan.tsv.tsv -> phylophlan.tsv)
11: A few remaining proteinortho output files are now copied also the proteinortho output folde
10: Critial typo fixed in mag_annotate__phylophlan (issue #23)
9: Changed magscot rules so that also empty output is taken now into consideration and does not throw an error anymore (issue #22)
8: Output bugfix in Phyophlan (two arguments, unnamed)
7: Bugfix that prevented Kraken2 from copying db files to faster disc spaces
6: Removed a non-public referene database (ciliates) from features.yaml (issue #17)
5: Added --memory {resources.mem_mb}  to the metaspades rule (issue #15)
4: Flag to turn on/off shm storage for kraken2 added
3: Summary scripts for Diamond runs adjusted
2: Problem with dnmd file ending solved
1: Critical bugfix for read_annotate__diamond

